rson_slug":"mehreen-faruqi","vote":"no"},{"name":"Michaelia Cash","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10707","person_slug":"michaelia-cash","vote":"no"},{"name":"Murray Watt","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10857","person_slug":"murray-watt","vote":"no"},{"name":"Nick McKim","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10841","person_slug":"nick-mckim","vote":"no"},{"name":"Patrick Dodson","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10846","person_slug":"patrick-dodson","vote":"no"},{"name":"Pauline Hanson","party":"One Nation","person_id":"tvfy_10280","person_slug":"pauline-hanson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Peter Georgiou","party":"One Nation","person_id":"tvfy_10898","person_slug":"peter-georgiou","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Peter Whish-Wilson","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10780","person_slug":"peter-whish-wilson","vote":"no"},{"name":"Rachel Siewert","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10584","person_slug":"rachel-siewert","vote":"no"},{"name":"Rex Patrick","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10903","person_slug":"rex-patrick","vote":"no"},{"name":"Richard Colbeck","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10131","person_slug":"richard-colbeck","vote":"no"},{"name":"Richard Di Natale","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10755","person_slug":"richard-di-natale","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stirling Griff","party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10851","person_slug":"stirling-griff","vote":"no"}],"name":"Motions - E-Cigarettes - Legalise liquid nicotine","noes":38,"question":"The majority voted against a [motion](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?id=2018-11-12.155.1) introduced by One Nation Senator [Peter Georgiou](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/wa/peter_georgiou) also on behalf of Senators [Leyonhjelm](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/nsw/david_leyonhjelm), [Hanson](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/queensland/pauline_hanson) and [Bernardi](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/sa/cory_bernardi). ### Motion text > *That the Senate—* > *(a) acknowledges that:* >> *(i) smoking is the largest preventable cause of death in Australia,* >> *(ii) successive Commonwealth Governments have used increased excise levels as the primary mechanism to deter smokers from maintaining their habit,* >> *(iii) there is growing evidence that vaping has helped many smokers to quit, and* >> *(iv) a growing number of countries, including the United Kingdom, Canada and New Zealand have already legalised vaping;* > *(b) notes that:* >> *(i) a recent Australian Institute of Health and Welfare survey found that, despite the Government's policy to reduce smoking rates, the national smoking rate had, in fact, not declined in the period 2013-16,* >> *(ii) last month, the CSIRO released a study confirming e-cigarettes assisted smokers in quitting,* >> *(iii) a poll conducted by the Australian Retailers Association showed 61% of Australians support the legalisation of vaping and e-cigarettes, and* >> *(iv) despite the above, under current Australian law, it is illegal to purchase, possess or use liquid nicotine for vaping without a prescription from a registered Australian medical practitioner; and* > *(c) calls on the Federal Government to immediately introduce legislation to legalise the sale, possession and use of liquid nicotine without restriction.*","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-5503","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2018-11-12/11"}
